To order thy desk, that it may be fit for use, heed these wise words:

First, cast off all clutter from the surface;
Then sweep with hand or broom of straw.
Next, set forth thy quill and inkwell nigh;
Thy pen shall rest in rest, not far from sight.
Place thy lamp aloft, that shadows flee away;
Let no dark spot disturb the light.

If books thou dost require, hang them on high,
So that their weight no longer crusheth thee.
